text:
C1 is confirmed: local-time conversion violates the function’s UTC contract and can assign visits to the wrong date. This is blocking.

C2 is confirmed: the test ignores date keys and lacks midnight boundary cases, so it misses the timezone bug. It should be fixed before merge.

```json
{
  "verdicts": [
    {
      "id": "C1",
      "verdict": "confirmed",
      "reason": "datetime.fromtimestamp(ts) uses the process's local timezone, so visits can receive incorrect date keys despite the documented UTC contract.",
      "evidence": ["app/visits.py:12", "app/visits.py:13"],
      "severity": "blocking"
    },
    {
      "id": "C2",
      "verdict": "confirmed",
      "reason": "The test uses noon UTC timestamps and asserts only counts, allowing incorrect timezone-derived date keys to pass undetected.",
      "evidence": ["tests/test_visits.py:9", "tests/test_visits.py:10", "tests/test_visits.py:11"],
      "severity": "should_fix"
    }
  ]
}
